From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:27:29 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 35/42] Plutonium: the dock's key hides what it shows in a
 thread just switched to

Switching threads gives the composer the keyboard, so a slot's thing
already showing in the new thread only got the keyboard back on its key,
and seemed to do nothing. Until the user types or clicks in the thread, the
key hides it. Going back never shows the slot's own thing again (it was
showing when the key was pressed): it puts the slot away.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
